  "contractsReviewed": [
    {
      "assessment": "The original child slot and a separate non-cleared anchor preserve one attempt. Frozen custody pins original actor, worker, image pin, lease object, path objects and identities, fence bytes, loop number/descriptor and binding. Popen/channel anchors and process identity remain retained through uncertainty and after closure.",
      "contract": "Original owner custody"
    },
    {
      "assessment": "Before stop the original ServiceChannel must be COMPLETED with its valid final frame, original exit0, both EOFs, no pending or trailing frame, completed input and original sequence/request identity. Native ordered closure and three-store/profile retirement are validated again through the existing child wire validator.",
      "contract": "Exact child completion"
    },
    {
      "assessment": "Worker-only membership and absence of nested cgroups are checked before STOP. The attempt is recorded before the unchanged generic stop can write/flush. Only its exact UNMOUNTED PID/token reply plus same worker exit0 authorizes finish. Generic finish is unchanged and its returned full receipt is required; stage or caller booleans cannot replace it.",
      "contract": "Normal stop and finish authority"
    },
    {
      "assessment": "A separate empty-members/no-child-cgroup check precedes the unchanged generic finish. Generic finish checks ownership, empty cgroup, original empty host target, one loop descriptor close, global image device/inode attachment inventory, ownership and cgroup again, cgroup removal, original fence unlink/parent fsync, then image lease close. New code does not duplicate this cleanup implementation.",
      "contract": "Cleanup order"
    },
    {
      "assessment": "Preflight failure, BUSY, uncertain STOP, AUTOCLEAR attachment persistence and any finish failure retain original state without automatic or new-ID cleanup replay. A stream-close exception after generic CLOSED restores the same retained owner and stays UNKNOWN; no finish receipt is invented.",
      "contract": "UNKNOWN and partial effects"
    },
    {
      "assessment": "Status and same-ID replay never invoke stop or finish. A new explicit close can start previously unattempted volume closure after deferred child completion. Once an original closure attempt exists, observation uses retained custody and does not call the RUNNING-only child path or released live-volume gate.",
      "contract": "Read-only observation"
    },
    {
      "assessment": "The server matches volumeClosure fields against the fresh original owner gate, requires child COMPLETED and all native/store/volume flags, and seals a detached canonical view before reply delivery. Cached CLOSED survives client loss; later status/replay checks actor/startTicks/token/service, original child and socket/parent identity before recovering it.",
      "contract": "External CLOSED"
    },
    {
      "assessment": "Exact bounded request schema and EOF framing, SO_PEERCRED, same owner/service preconditions, never-evicted bounded mutation IDs, original server/socket identity and pre-effect dispatch markers remain in force after CLOSED. Listener close only closes the listener descriptor and keeps socket path and proof.",
      "contract": "Request and endpoint continuity"
    },
    {
      "assessment": "New tests execute real Unix socket/peer checks, Node client/CLI and synthetic child Popen/pipes. The unchanged generic stop/finish/_owned/_empty_scope/_sync_parent and kernel _members bodies run through explicit worker/cgroup/mount/loop/lease ports and temporary files. These ports do not establish a mounted or installed native service.",
      "contract": "Source fixture fidelity and limits"
    },
    {
      "assessment": "Old R163 expectations were narrowly updated for the integrated close path: read-only child completion still cannot clean up; old pipe-only CLI fixtures now explicitly fail worker-only preflight and observe retained UNKNOWN. New R164 fixtures cover successful closure. The unchanged old Python CLI wrapper is intentionally archived alongside five changed old test/support files.",
      "contract": "Prior regression updates"
    }
  ],
